# What `gcloud builds submit .` uploads for the Cloud Run image (editions/gcp/deploy/deploy.ps1 / deploy.sh).
# Everything in .gitignore stays local (generated worlds, .venv, caches, models); so do the parts of the
# repository the image does not use. The Dockerfile reads: pyproject.toml uv.lock README.md LICENSE src ui
# .streamlit data/docs evals editions/gcp.
.gcloudignore
.git
.gitignore
#!include:.gitignore
.claude/
.agents/
.cache/
.github/
tests/
pitch/
scripts/
docs/
editions/snowflake/
editions/amd/
data/golden/
data/docs/raw/
